openapi: 3.0.3
info:
  title: Unravel Carbon Public API
  version: "1.0.0"
  description: |

    # Welcome to Unravel Carbon API

    The **Unravel Carbon Public API** empowers organizations to seamlessly access, analyze, and integrate comprehensive carbon emissions data into their sustainability workflows.

    ## Quick Start Guide

     **Get Your API Key**:
       - Log in to your [Unravel dashboard](https://app.unravelcarbon.com/)
       - Navigate to [Integrations](https://app.unravelcarbon.com/integrations)
       - Create a new API key

    ## Authentication

    All API endpoints require authentication using **Bearer tokens**. Include your API key in the Authorization header:

    `
    Authorization: Bearer your_api_key_here
    `

    ## What You Can Do

    - **Raw Data Access**: Retrieve granular emissions data with advanced filtering options
    - **Aggregated Analytics**: Get summarized insights with flexible grouping and calculations
    - **Real-time Sync**: Check for data updates to keep your systems synchronized  
    - **Metadata Management**: Access facility structures and emission categories
    - **Export Capabilities**: Download data in JSON or CSV formats for further analysis
    - **Direct Data Ingestion**: Upload data directly using the API for automatic processing.
    - **Access audit reports**: Export active user listings, user-to-role mappings, role-to-function matrices, and privileged access activity history for IT access reviews.

    ## Common Use Cases

    - **Sustainability Reporting**: Generate periodic emissions reports by facility or category
    - **Supply Chain Analysis**: Track emissions by supplier and spend category
    - **Trend Analysis**: Monitor emissions changes over time with update tracking
    - **Data Integration**: Sync emissions data with business intelligence tools
    - **Compliance Monitoring**: Export data for regulatory reporting requirements

    ## Response Formats

    - **JSON** (default): Structured data for programmatic access
    - **CSV**: Download links for spreadsheet analysis and reporting

    ## Rate Limits

    - **Standard**: 20 requests per minute (sliding window)
    - Rate limit headers are included in all responses
    - Recommended minimum interval: **5 seconds per request**

    ## Data Types & Emission Categories

    The API supports various emission data types, each with specific fields:

    | Data Type | Description | Fields |
    |-----------|-------------|------------|
    | `trx` | Transaction data | `_id`, `updated_at`, `date`, `scope`, `total_emission`, `scope_category`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_PGS`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_GOODS`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_NRG`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_U_TRANS`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_WASTE`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_BUSINESS`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_EMPLOY`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_U_LEASE`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_D_TRANS`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_PROCESS_SOLD`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_USE_SOLD`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_END_LIFE`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_D_LEASE`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_FRANCHISE`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_INVEST`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_S3`, `transaction_id`, `secondary_transaction_id`, `business_model`, `item_description`, `supplier`, `total_price`, `currency`, `units`, `unit_emission`, `item_emission_factor_unit`, `spend_category`, `match`, `product_category`, `product_subcategory`, `material_composition_breakdown`, `capital_goods`, `act_measure_unit`, `act_measure_value`, `item_unit_weight`, `trans_distance`, `manufacturer_name`, `manufacturer_location_of_origin`, `item_ef_source`, `item_ef_name`, `item_match_granularity`, `item_location_granularity`, `business_facility_name`, `file_name`, `company` |
    | `emp_com` | Employee commuting | `_id`, `updated_at`, `begin_date`, `end_date`, `identifier`, `num_employee`, `wfh_pct`, `avg_distance`, `date`, `scope`, `total_emission`, `scope_category`, `employee_number`, `wfh_perc`, `roundtrip_dist`, `car_perc`, `bicl_perc`, `bus_perc`, `train_perc`, `moto_perc`, `taxi_perc`, `walk_perc`, `car_ef`, `bicl_ef`, `bus_ef`, `train_ef`, `moto_ef`, `taxi_ef`, `walk_ef`, `office_days`, `bicl_emission`, `bus_emission`, `car_emission`, `moto_emission`, `taxi_emission`, `train_emission`, `walk_emission`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_EMPLOY`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_S3`, `country`, `file_name`, `business_facility_name`, `company` |
    | `biz_travel_air` | Business travel (air) | `_id`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `date`, `scope`, `total_emission`, `scope_category`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_S3`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_BUSINESS`, `trip_id`, `unit_emission`, `air_class`, `departure_latlong`, `departure_location`, `destination_location`, `destination_latlong`, `distance`, `haul`, `trip_type`, `file_name`, `business_facility_name`, `company` |
    | `biz_travel_hotel` | Business travel (hotel) | `_id`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `date`, `scope`, `total_emission`, `scope_category`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_S3`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_BUSINESS`, `trip_id`, `unit_emission`, `city`, `city_used`, `country`, `hotel_nights`, `hotel_type`, `return_date`, `company`, `file_name`, `business_facility_name` |
    | `biz_travel_land` | Business travel (land) | `_id`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `date`, `scope`, `total_emission`, `scope_category`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_S3`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_BUSINESS`, `trip_id`, `unit_emission`, `destination_city`, `destination_country`, `distance`, `distance_derived`, `distance_unit`, `fuel_capacity`, `fuel_type`, `origin_city`, `origin_country`, `travel_mode`, `trip_type`, `company`, `file_name`, `business_facility_name` |
    | `transport` | Transportation & logistics | `_id`, `updated_at`, `scope`, `total_emission`, `scope_category`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_U_TRANS`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_D_TRANS`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_S3`, `transport_id`, `transport_type`, `supplier_name`, `transport_mode`, `weight_of_goods`, `normalized_transport_mode`, `calc_type`, `co2_d_trans`, `co2_u_trans`, `co2_s3`, `total_distance`, `total_number_of_trips`, `end_date`, `begin_date`, `file_name`, `business_facility_name`, `company` |
    | `use_end` | End-of-life treatment | `_id`, `updated_at`, `scope`, `total_emission`, `scope_category`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_S3`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_END_LIFE`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_USE_SOLD`, `record_id`, `product_category`, `product_subcategory`, `quantity`, `average_unit_weight`, `country`, `waste_type`, `waste_name`, `waste_landf_perc`, `waste_inc_perc`, `waste_comp_perc`, `waste_recl_perc`, `waste_landf_ef`, `waste_inc_ef`, `waste_comp_ef`, `waste_recl_ef`, `waste_ef`, `begin_date`, `end_date`, `company`, `file_name`, `business_facility_name` |
    | `use_sold` | Use of sold products | `_id`, `updated_at`, `scope`, `total_emission`, `scope_category`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_S3`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_END_LIFE`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_USE_SOLD`, `record_id`, `product_category`, `product_subcategory`, `quantity`, `average_unit_weight`, `country`, `energy_consumption`, `ref_weight`, `ef_scope2`, `begin_date`, `end_date`, `company`, `file_name`, `business_facility_name` |
    | `refrigerant` | Refrigerant emissions | `_id`, `updated_at`, `begin_date`, `end_date`, `identifier`, `transaction_id`, `application`, `equipment_type`, `within_op_control`, `refrigerant_type`, `ac_gross_floor_area`, `area_unit`, `recharged_amount`, `date`, `scope`, `scope_category`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.S1_IND`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_S1`, `gwp`, `default_application`, `refrigerant_leakage`, `stock_diff`, `avg_charge`, `cop`, `refrigeration_power`, `leak_rate`, `units`, `total_emission`, `business_facility_name`, `company`, `file_name` |
    | `leased_space_asset` | Leased space assets | `_id`, `updated_at`, `begin_date`, `end_date`, `identifier`, `stream_type`, `space_type`, `name`, `electricity_used`, `fuel_type`, `amount_of_fuel`, `scope`, `total_emission`, `scope_category`, `date`, `calc_type`, `co2_d_lease`, `scope1_nrg_value`, `ef_scope1`, `fuel_emissions`, `electricity_emissions`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_D_LEASE`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_S3`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_U_LEASE`, `space_electricity_consumption_sqm_day`, `space_employee`, `co2_s3`, `business_facility_name`, `company`, `file_name` |
    | `leased_vehicle_asset` | Leased vehicle assets | `_id`, `begin_date`, `end_date`, `identifier`, `stream_type`, `vehicle_type`, `vehicle_model`, `fuel_type`, `num_of_vehicles`, `total_energy_consumption`, `total_distance_travelled`, `scope`, `total_emission`, `scope_category`, `date`, `calc_type`, `co2_d_lease`, `ef_scope1`, `vehicle_data_type`, `fuel_name`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_D_LEASE`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_S3`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_U_LEASE`, `fuel_emissions`, `co2_s3`, `electricity_emissions`, `business_facility_name`, `company`, `file_name` |
    | `scope1_fuel` | Scope 1 fuel combustion | `_id`, `updated_at`, `scope`, `total_emission`, `scope_category`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.S1_FUEL`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_S1`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_NRG`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_S3`, `begin_date`, `end_date`, `fuel_type`, `quantity`, `unit_of_measurement`, `fuel_name`, `nrg_value`, `ef_scope3_cat3`, `spend_cat`, `ef_type`, `unit`, `fuel_category`, `fuel_density`, `fuel_density_unit`, `item_granularity`, `match_granularity`, `location_granularity`, `ef_category`, `energy_amount_gj`, `fuel_ef_co2_co2e`, `fuel_ef_ch4_co2e`, `fuel_ef_n2o_co2e`, `ef_item`, `fuel_emissions_co2_co2e`, `fuel_emissions_ch4_co2e`, `fuel_emissions_n2o_co2e`, `calc_type`, `business_facility_name`, `company`, `file_name` |
    | `scope2_electricity` | Scope 2 purchased electricity | `_id`, `updated_at`, `scope`, `update_job`, `total_emission`, `scope_category`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.S2_ELEC`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_S2`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_NRG`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_S3`, `begin_date`, `end_date`, `item_granularity`, `match_granularity`, `location_granularity`, `ef_category`, `s2_elec_loc`, `s2_elec_gef`, `s2_elec_gef_after_rec`, `grid_electricity_quantity`, `low_carbon_electricity_quantity`, `ef_country`, `ef_scope2`, `ef_unit`, `transmission_distribution_loss_pct`, `spend_cat`, `ef_type`, `location_quantity`, `calc_type`, `company`, `file_name`, `business_facility_name` |
    | `scope2_heat_cold` | Scope 2 heat/cold | `_id`, `updated_at`, `scope`, `total_emission`, `scope_category`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_S2`, `sub_scope_cat_dict.S2_HEAT`, `begin_date`, `end_date`, `medium_type`, `quantity`, `unit_of_measurement`, `raw_quantity`, `raw_unit_of_measurement`, `unit_conversion_factor`, `emission_factor`, `company`, `file_name`, `business_facility_name` |

    ## Aggregated Data Fields

    The aggregated data endpoint supports the following fields for analysis:

    | Field | Type | Description |
    |-------|------|-------------|
    | `date` | string | Date of the emission record (YYYY-MM-DD) |
    | `year` | integer | Year derived from date |
    | `month` | string | Month derived from date (YYYY-MM format) |
    | `quarter` | integer | Quarter derived from date (1-4) |
    | `file_name` | string | Original file name |
    | `business_facility_name` | string | Business facility name |
    | `subfacility_code` | string | Subfacility code (nullable) |
    | `company` | string | Company name |
    | `uploader` | string | Email of user who uploaded the file |
    | `total_emission` | number | Total emission value |
    | `data_type` | string | Data type of the emission record |
    | `scope_category` | string | Scope category |
    | `city` | string | City name |
    | `country` | string | Country name |

    ## Company Context

    All API requests are scoped to your organization's data. The API automatically filters results based on your API key's associated company.

    ## Pagination

    Most endpoints support pagination with `page` and `limit` parameters:
    - `page`: Page number (default: 1)
    - `limit`: Items per page (default: 100, max: 1000)

    ## Currency Codes

    For fields that require currency codes (e.g., `currency` field in PGS data), use 3-letter ISO 4217 currency codes. Refer to the [complete list of valid currency codes](https://www.iban.com/currency-codes) for supported values.

servers:
  - url: https://api.unravelcarbon.com/api/v1

tags:
  - name: Analytics & Reporting
    description: Raw emissions data retrieval, aggregated data, analytics, and bulk export capabilities
  - name: Data Ingestion
    description: Submit and ingest emissions data directly via API
  - name: Reference & Metadata
    description: Facilities, categories, and system configuration data
  - name: Admin
    description: Company administration exports for IT access reviews (active users, role assignments, permissions, and privileged account activity)

components:
  securitySchemes:
    BearerAuth:
      type: http
      scheme: bearer
      bearerFormat: JWT

  parameters:
    Authorization:
      name: Authorization
      in: header
      description: Bearer token (API Key)
      required: true
      schema:
        type: string
        example: Bearer <your_api_key>

  responses:
    UnauthorizedError:
      description: Authentication failed
      content:
        application/json:
          schema:
            $ref: "#/components/schemas/Error"
          example:
            error: Invalid API key.

    AuditUnauthorizedError:
      description: |
        Missing, invalid, or expired API key, or a valid key whose owner is not currently a company or workspace Administrator.

        These cases return 401 with a `message` field. A valid non-admin key does not return 403.
      content:
        application/json:
          schema:
            type: object
            properties:
              message:
                type: string
          examples:
            invalidKey:
              value:
                message: Invalid API key.
            notAdmin:
              summary: Valid API key whose owner is not currently an admin
              value:
                message: Authentication failed

    BadRequestError:
      description: Invalid request or parameters
      content:
        application/json:
          schema:
            $ref: "#/components/schemas/Error"
          example:
            error: "Invalid query parameters: limit must be > 0"

  schemas:
    Error:
      type: object
      properties:
        error:
          type: string

    EmissionRawRecord:
      type: object
      properties:
        _id: { type: string, example: "689efca0ff6d9052499764cb" }
        updated_at:
          {
            type: string,
            format: date-time,
            example: "2025-08-15 09:23:44.605000",
          }
        date:
          { type: string, format: date-time, example: "2024-02-01 00:00:00" }
        begin_date: { type: string, format: date-time, nullable: true }
        end_date: { type: string, format: date-time, nullable: true }
        scope: { type: integer, example: 3 }
        total_emission: { type: number, example: 39.61534179891021 }
        scope_category: { type: string, example: "NA" }
        sub_scope_cat_dict:
          type: object
          additionalProperties: true
          description: Sub-scope category emissions dictionary
        transaction_id: { type: string, example: "38412847182318237.505663970" }
        secondary_transaction_id: { type: string, example: "505663970" }
        business_model: { type: string, example: "Indent" }
        item_description: { type: string, example: "Crew Fashion T-Shirts" }
        supplier: { type: string, example: "64a9483931a5c3dd041a0138" }
        total_price: { type: number, example: 23.885944614465927 }
        currency:
          {
            type: string,
            example: "USD",
            description: "3-letter ISO currency code. See [valid currency codes](https://www.iban.com/currency-codes)",
          }
        units: { type: number, example: 1.0 }
        unit_emission: { type: number, example: 1.658521044 }
        item_emission_factor_unit: { type: string, example: "kg CO2-e/USD" }
        spend_category:
          { type: string, example: "Textiles and textile products" }
        match: { type: string, example: "exiobase" }
        product_category: { type: string, example: "Clothing - Men" }
        product_subcategory: { type: string, example: "" }
        material_composition_breakdown:
          type: array
          items: { type: string }
          example: []
        capital_goods: { type: boolean, example: false }
        act_measure_unit: { type: string, example: "PC" }
        act_measure_value: { type: number, example: 293.0 }
        item_unit_weight: { type: number, example: 0.15 }
        trans_distance: { type: number, example: 0.0 }
        manufacturer_name: { type: string, example: "Adidas" }
        manufacturer_location_of_origin: { type: string, example: "Singapore" }
        item_ef_source: { type: string, example: "411" }
        item_ef_name: { type: string, example: "Wearing apparel; furs" }
        item_match_granularity: { type: string, example: "category" }
        item_location_granularity: { type: string, example: "continent" }
        business_facility_name: { type: string, example: "Mercutio Office" }
        file_name: { type: string, example: "" }
        company: { type: string, example: "Alpha Squad Inc" }
        uploader: { type: string, example: "system@unravelcarbon.com" }
      additionalProperties: true

    CSVExportResponse:
      type: object
      description: CSV export response containing download information
      required:
        - status
      properties:
        download_url:
          type: string
          description: Direct download URL for the CSV file (when processing is complete)
          example: "https://s3.amazonaws.com/bucket/emissions_export_20240115.csv"
        status:
          type: string
          enum: [complete, processing]
          description: Status of the CSV export
          example: "complete"
        task_id:
          type: string
          description: Task ID for tracking async exports (when status is 'processing')
          example: "abc123def456"
        message:
          type: string
          description: Status message or instructions
          example: "CSV export completed successfully"

    EmissionRawResponse:
      type: object
      properties:
        data:
          type: array
          items:
            $ref: "#/components/schemas/EmissionRawRecord"
        count:
          type: integer
          example: 1
        page:
          type: integer
          example: 1
        limit:
          type: integer
          example: 100

    AggregatedEmissionRecord:
      type: object
      properties:
        city: { type: string, example: "Paris" }
        category: { type: string, example: "Retail" }
        business_facility_name: { type: string, example: "Alpha France" }
        spend_category: { type: string, example: "Pulp and paper" }
        total_emission: { type: number, example: 77.33 }
      additionalProperties: true

    AggregatedEmissionResponse:
      type: object
      properties:
        data:
          type: array
          items:
            $ref: "#/components/schemas/AggregatedEmissionRecord"
        count:
          type: integer
          example: 175
        format:
          type: string
          example: json

    DataAggregationRequest:
      type: object
      required: [columns]
      properties:
        columns:
          type: array
          items:
            type: string
            enum:
              - total_emission
              - scope_category
              - data_type
              - date
              - file_name
              - uploader
              - month
              - year
              - quarter
              - business_facility_name
              - city
              - country
              - company
              - subfacility_code
          description: Columns to include in response
          default: []
        format:
          type: string
          enum: [json, csv]
          default: json
          description: Export format
        per_page:
          type: integer
          minimum: 1
          maximum: 1000
          default: 100
          description: Number of records per page
        page:
          type: integer
          minimum: 1
          default: 1
          description: Page number for pagination
        sort_by:
          type: string
          enum:
            - total_emission
            - scope_category
            - data_type
            - date
            - file_name
            - uploader
            - month
            - year
            - quarter
            - business_facility_name
            - city
            - country
            - company
          description: Field to sort by
        sort_order:
          type: string
          enum: [asc, desc]
          default: asc
          description: Sort order
        # Top-level filter parameters
        scope:
          type: array
          items:
            type: integer
            minimum: 1
            maximum: 3
          description: Filter by emission scope (1, 2, 3)
        data_type:
          type: array
          items:
            type: string
          description: Filter by data type
        scope_category:
          type: array
          items:
            type: string
          description: Filter by scope category
        business_facility_name:
          type: array
          items:
            type: string
          description: Filter by business facility name
        subfacility_code:
          type: array
          items:
            type: string
          description: Filter by subfacility code
        file_name:
          type: array
          items:
            type: string
          description: Filter by file name
        uploader:
          type: array
          items:
            type: string
          description: Filter by uploaded from email
        date_from:
          type: string
          format: date
          description: Filter by start date
        date_to:
          type: string
          format: date
          description: Filter by end date

    DataAggregationRecord:
      type: object
      properties:
        date:
          type: string
          format: date
          example: "2025-01-13"
          description: Date of the emission record
        year:
          type: integer
          example: 2025
          description: Year derived from date
        month:
          type: string
          example: "2025-01"
          description: Month derived from date (YYYY-MM format)
        quarter:
          type: integer
          example: 1
          description: Quarter derived from date (1-4)
        file_name:
          type: string
          example: "uc_20250603062403.csv"
          description: Original file name
        business_facility_name:
          type: string
          example: "UC_CORP"
          description: Business facility name
        company:
          type: string
          example: "Demo Corporation"
          description: Company name
        uploader:
          type: string
          example: "system@unravelcarbon.com"
          description: Email of user who uploaded the file
        total_emission:
          type: number
          example: 0.7749856676879998
          description: Total emission value
        data_type:
          type: string
          example: "scope2_electricity"
          description: Data type of the emission record
        scope_category:
          type: string
          example: "Fuel and energy related"
          description: Scope category
        city:
          type: string
          nullable: true
          example: "None"
          description: City name
        country:
          type: string
          example: "Singapore"
          description: Country name
        subfacility_code:
          type: string
          nullable: true
          example: "BF0"
          description: Subfacility code
      additionalProperties: true

    DataAggregationResponse:
      type: object
      properties:
        data:
          type: array
          items:
            $ref: "#/components/schemas/DataAggregationRecord"
          description: Array of aggregated emission records
        count:
          type: integer
          example: 27
          description: Total number of records
        page:
          type: integer
          example: 1
          description: Current page number
        per_page:
          type: integer
          example: 1
          description: Number of records per page
        format:
          type: string
          example: json
          description: Response format

    UpdateStatusRecord:
      type: object
      properties:
        facility_id: { type: string, example: "abc123" }
        date: { type: string, format: date, example: "2023-03-15" }
        has_updates: { type: boolean, example: true }
        last_updated_at:
          { type: string, format: date-time, example: "2023-03-16T10:00:00Z" }

    UpdateStatusResponse:
      type: object
      properties:
        data:
          type: array
          items:
            $ref: "#/components/schemas/UpdateStatusRecord"

    Facility:
      type: object
      properties:
        id: { type: string, example: "abc123" }
        name: { type: string, example: "Headquarters" }
        category: { type: string, example: "company" }
        parent: { type: string, nullable: true }
        children:
          type: array
          items:
            $ref: "#/components/schemas/Facility"

    FacilityResponse:
      type: object
      properties:
        data:
          type: array
          items:
            $ref: "#/components/schemas/Facility"

    EmissionCategory:
      type: object
      required: ["scope", "category", "data_types"]
      properties:
        scope:
          description: Emission scope or scopes covered by the listed data types.
          oneOf:
            - type: string
              example: "S1"
            - type: array
              items: { type: string }
              example: ["S1", "S2", "S3"]
        category:
          type: array
          items: { type: string }
          example: ["Fuel combustion", "Fuel and energy related"]
        data_types:
          type: array
          items: { type: string }
          example: ["scope1_fuel"]

    EmissionCategoryResponse:
      type: object
      properties:
        data:
          type: array
          items:
            $ref: "#/components/schemas/EmissionCategory"

    AuditActiveUserRecord:
      type: object
      description: One row per active company user.
      properties:
        Name: { type: string, example: "Ada Admin" }
        Status: { type: string, enum: [Active], example: "Active" }
        UserPrincipalName: { type: string, example: "ada@example.com" }
        Company Level:
          type: string
          description: Comma-separated organizational unit names assigned to the user.
          example: "HQ, Nike France"
        Role:
          type: string
          description: "Paired org and role assignments in OrgName-Role format, comma-separated."
          example: "HQ: Admin, Nike France: Viewer"
        Subsystem: { type: string, enum: [ESG], example: "ESG" }
        Load Date:
          type: string
          description: Report generation date (`dd/MM/yyyy`).
          example: "28/08/2026"
        Last Login Date:
          type: string
          description: Last login date (`dd/MM/yyyy`), blank when never logged in.
          example: "15/08/2026"

    AuditActiveUserResponse:
      type: object
      properties:
        data:
          type: array
          items:
            $ref: "#/components/schemas/AuditActiveUserRecord"

    AuditUserToRoleRecord:
      type: object
      description: One row per user, role, and organizational unit (U2R grain).
      properties:
        UserID:
          type: string
          description: SSO login email. Same value as `UserEmail`.
          example: "ada@example.com"
        User: { type: string, example: "Ada Admin" }
        UserEmail: { type: string, example: "ada@example.com" }
        Department:
          type: string
          description: Always blank.
          example: ""
        Rolename: { type: string, example: "Admin" }
        Created:
          type: string
          description: Role assignment created date (`dd/MM/yyyy`) from the live `UserRole` (or invitation / deleted snapshot for inactive rows).
          example: "01/01/2026"
        Modified:
          type: string
          description: Role assignment last modified date (`dd/MM/yyyy`) from the live `UserRole` (or invitation / deleted snapshot for inactive rows).
          example: "15/08/2026"
        CreatedBy:
          type: string
          description: Email of the user who created the assignment. Blank when unknown.
          example: "admin@example.com"
        ModifiedBy:
          type: string
          description: Email of the user who last changed the assignment. Blank when unknown.
          example: "admin@example.com"
        LastLoginDateTime:
          type: string
          description: Last login timestamp (`dd/MM/yyyy HH:mm:ss`), blank when never logged in.
          example: "15/08/2026 09:30:00"
        LastLogoutDateTime:
          type: string
          description: Last logout timestamp (`dd/MM/yyyy HH:mm:ss`), blank when never logged out.
          example: "15/08/2026 17:00:00"
        User Active Status (0 equal inactive, 1 equal active):
          type: integer
          enum: [0, 1]
          description: |
            `1` for users with a live `UserRole` assignment.
            `0` for inactive rows: pending invitations (Invite Sent and Invite Expired)
            and the latest deleted-user snapshot per email.
          example: 1
        User Role Active Status (0 equal inactive, 1 equal active):
          type: integer
          enum: [0, 1]
          description: Mirrors user active status for each U2R row.
          example: 1

    AuditUserToRoleResponse:
      type: object
      properties:
        data:
          type: array
          items:
            $ref: "#/components/schemas/AuditUserToRoleRecord"

    AuditRolePermissionRecord:
      type: object
      description: One row per role and permission claim (R2F grain).
      properties:
        RoleName: { type: string, enum: [Admin, Editor, Viewer], example: "Admin" }
        FunctionCode: { type: string, example: "invite:user" }
        FunctionDescription: { type: string, example: "invite:user" }
        Role Active Status (0 equal inactive, 1 equal active):
          type: integer
          enum: [0, 1]
          example: 1
        Created:
          type: string
          description: Always blank (current-state matrix only).
          example: ""
        Modified:
          type: string
          description: Always blank (current-state matrix only).
          example: ""
        CreatedBy:
          type: string
          description: Always blank (current-state matrix only).
          example: ""
        ModifiedBy:
          type: string
          description: Always blank (current-state matrix only).
          example: ""

    AuditRolePermissionResponse:
      type: object
      properties:
        data:
          type: array
          items:
            $ref: "#/components/schemas/AuditRolePermissionRecord"

    AuditEventRecord:
      type: object
      description: One privileged access audit event.
      properties:
        Performed By (UserID):
          type: string
          description: Performer email address.
          example: "admin@example.com"
        Performed By (UserName):
          type: string
          description: Performer display name.
          example: "Ada Admin"
        Applied on account / role / configuration:
          type: string
          description: Target account, role, or configuration affected by the activity.
          example: "ada@example.com"
        Activity Type:
          type: string
          enum:
            - login
            - logout
            - password_update
            - admin-invite-user
            - admin-delete-user
            - admin-update-user-role
            - admin-update-user-org_struct
          example: "admin-invite-user"
        Old Value:
          type: string
          description: Previous value for update and delete activities, blank otherwise.
          example: "HQ: Viewer"
        New Value:
          type: string
          description: New value for invite and update activities, blank otherwise.
          example: "HQ: Admin"
        Created Date / Time UTC (dd/MM/yyyy HH:mm:ss):
          type: string
          description: Event timestamp in UTC (`dd/MM/yyyy HH:mm:ss`).
          example: "28/08/2026 09:30:00"

    AuditEventResponse:
      type: object
      properties:
        data:
          type: array
          items:
            $ref: "#/components/schemas/AuditEventRecord"
        page:
          type: integer
          example: 1
        limit:
          type: integer
          example: 100
        total:
          type: integer
          description: Total matching events for the query (before pagination).
          example: 250

    ElectricityRecord:
      type: object
      required: ["transaction_id", "date", "consumption_kwh", "facility_name"]
      properties:
        transaction_id:
          type: string
          description: Unique identifier for deduplication
          pattern: "^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+$"
          maxLength: 100
          example: "ELEC_01_2024_01_1"
        date:
          type: string
          format: date
          description: Date of electricity consumption (YYYY-MM-DD format)
          example: "2024-01-16"
        consumption_kwh:
          type: number
          minimum: 0
          maximum: 999999999
          description: Electricity consumption in kilowatt-hours
          example: 1150.5
        facility_name:
          type: string
          description: Facility name where consumption occurred
          maxLength: 200
          example: "Alpha Llama Lima HQ"
        subfacility_code:
          type: string
          description: Subfacility code (optional)
          maxLength: 100
          example: "BF0"
        supplier_name:
          type: string
          description: Electricity supplier name (optional)
          maxLength: 200
          example: "Supplier A"

    ElectricityIngestRequest:
      type: object
      required: ["records"]
      properties:
        records:
          type: array
          items:
            $ref: "#/components/schemas/ElectricityRecord"
          minItems: 1
          maxItems: 1000
          description: Array of electricity consumption records

    FacilityProcessed:
      type: object
      properties:
        facility_name:
          type: string
          description: Name of the facility
          example: "Alpha Llama Lima HQ"
        status:
          type: string
          enum: ["processed", "created", "updated"]
          description: Processing status for this facility
          example: "updated"
        records_count:
          type: integer
          description: Number of records processed for this facility
          example: 4
        total_consumption_kwh:
          type: number
          description: Total electricity consumption for this facility
          example: 4602.0
        date_range:
          type: object
          properties:
            start_date:
              type: string
              format: date
              example: "2024-01-16"
            end_date:
              type: string
              format: date
              example: "2024-01-19"

    ElectricityIngestSummary:
      type: object
      properties:
        total_facilities:
          type: integer
          description: Total number of facilities processed
          example: 1
        total_records:
          type: integer
          description: Total number of records processed across all facilities
          example: 4
        total_consumption_kwh:
          type: number
          description: Total electricity consumption across all facilities
          example: 4602.0
        new_facilities:
          type: array
          items:
            type: string
          description: List of facility names that were newly created
          example: []
        existing_facilities:
          type: array
          items:
            type: string
          description: List of facility names that already existed
          example: ["Alpha Llama Lima HQ"]
        date_range:
          type: object
          properties:
            start_date:
              type: string
              format: date
              example: "2024-01-16"
            end_date:
              type: string
              format: date
              example: "2024-01-19"

    ElectricityIngestResponse:
      type: object
      properties:
        status:
          type: string
          enum: ["success"]
          description: Processing status
          example: "success"
        message:
          type: string
          description: Success message
          example: "Successfully processed electricity data for 1 facilities"
        data:
          type: object
          properties:
            facilities_processed:
              type: array
              items:
                $ref: "#/components/schemas/FacilityProcessed"
            summary:
              $ref: "#/components/schemas/ElectricityIngestSummary"
            next_steps:
              type: array
              items:
                type: string
              description: Helpful next steps for the user
              example:
                [
                  "Your scope2 electricity data has been successfully uploaded",
                  "Carbon calculations will be processed automatically",
                  "You can view results in your dashboard within 5-10 minutes",
                  "Check your email for processing confirmation",
                ]

    ErrorResponse:
      type: object
      properties:
        status:
          type: string
          enum: ["error"]
          description: Error status
        message:
          type: string
          description: Error message
        errors:
          type: array
          items:
            type: object
            properties:
              field:
                type: string
                description: Field that caused the error
              message:
                type: string
                description: Error message for this field
        help:
          type: string
          description: Helpful guidance for resolving the error

    PurchaseGoodsAndServicesRecord:
      type: object
      required:
        [
          "transaction_id",
          "transaction_date",
          "facility_name",
          "item_description",
          "transaction_amount",
          "currency",
          "supplier_name",
          "supplier_location",
        ]
      properties:
        transaction_id:
          type: string
          description: Unique identifier for deduplication
          pattern: "^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+$"
          maxLength: 100
          example: "PGS_001_2024_01_15"
        transaction_date:
          type: string
          format: date
          description: Date of the transaction (YYYY-MM-DD format)
          example: "2024-01-15"
        facility_name:
          type: string
          description: Facility name where the transaction occurred
          maxLength: 200
          example: "Main Office"
        item_description:
          type: string
          description: Description of the purchased item or service
          maxLength: 500
          example: "Office Supplies - Notebooks and Pens"
        transaction_amount:
          type: number
          description: Total transaction amount
          example: 1250.50
        supplier_name:
          type: string
          description: Supplier name
          maxLength: 200
          example: "Office Depot Inc"
        supplier_location:
          type: string
          description: Location of the supplier (required if supplier_name is provided)
          maxLength: 200
          example: "New York, USA"
        currency:
          type: string
          description: Currency code (3-letter ISO format, will be uppercased)
          pattern: "^[A-Za-z]{3}$"
          example: "USD"
        activity_measure_value:
          type: integer
          description: Quantity/amount of activity (must be paired with activity_measure_unit)
          example: 150
        activity_measure_unit:
          type: string
          description: Unit of measurement for activity (must be paired with activity_measure_value)
          maxLength: 50
          example: "kilograms"
        item_unit_price:
          type: number
          description: Price per unit
          example: 119.99
        item_unit_weight_kg:
          type: number
          description: Weight per unit in kilograms
          example: 2.5
        product_category:
          type: string
          description: Category of the product
          maxLength: 200
          example: "Electronics"
        product_sub_category:
          type: string
          description: Subcategory of the product
          maxLength: 200
          example: "Laptops"
        material_composition:
          type: string
          description: Material composition breakdown
          maxLength: 500
          example: "50% plastic, 30% metal, 20% electronics"
        general_ledger_act:
          type: string
          description: General ledger account code
          maxLength: 100
          example: "6000-001"

    PurchaseGoodsAndServicesIngestRequest:
      type: object
      required: ["records"]
      properties:
        records:
          type: array
          items:
            $ref: "#/components/schemas/PurchaseGoodsAndServicesRecord"
          minItems: 1
          maxItems: 1000
          description: Array of purchase goods and services records

    PurchaseGoodsAndServicesIngestResponse:
      type: object
      properties:
        status:
          type: string
          enum: ["success"]
          description: Processing status
          example: "success"
        message:
          type: string
          description: Success message
          example: "Successfully processed 2 records across 1 facilities"
        data:
          type: object
          properties:
            sync_run_id:
              type: string
              description: Unique identifier for this sync run
              example: "6937e5891dcdfab34c7a3cd2"
            import_type:
              type: string
              description: Type of import
              example: "purchase_goods_and_services"
            total_records:
              type: integer
              description: Total number of records processed
              example: 2
            facilities_processed:
              type: array
              items:
                type: object
                properties:
                  facility_name:
                    type: string
                    description: Name of the facility
                    example: "Huskies of Norway"
                  records_count:
                    type: integer
                    description: Number of records processed for this facility
                    example: 2
                  status:
                    type: string
                    description: Processing status for this facility
                    example: "success"
                  date_range:
                    type: object
                    properties:
                      start_date:
                        type: string
                        format: date
                        example: "2024-01-09"
                      end_date:
                        type: string
                        format: date
                        example: "2024-01-10"
            upload_jobs_created:
              type: integer
              description: Number of upload jobs created
              example: 1
            upload_job_ids:
              type: array
              items:
                type: string
              description: List of upload job IDs
              example: ["6937e5891dcdfab34c7a3cd3"]
            summary:
              type: object
              properties:
                total_facilities:
                  type: integer
                  description: Total number of facilities processed
                  example: 1
                total_records:
                  type: integer
                  description: Total number of records processed
                  example: 2
                successful_facilities:
                  type: integer
                  description: Number of facilities processed successfully
                  example: 1
                failed_facilities:
                  type: integer
                  description: Number of facilities that failed processing
                  example: 0
                date_range:
                  type: object
                  properties:
                    start_date:
                      type: string
                      format: date
                      example: "2024-01-09"
                    end_date:
                      type: string
                      format: date
                      example: "2024-01-10"

    Scope1FuelRecord:
      type: object
      required:
        [
          "transaction_id",
          "start_date",
          "end_date",
          "facility_name",
          "fuel_type",
          "quantity",
          "unit_of_measurement",
        ]
      properties:
        transaction_id:
          type: string
          description: Unique identifier for deduplication
          pattern: "^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+$"
          maxLength: 100
          example: "FUEL_001_2024_01_15"
        start_date:
          type: string
          format: date
          description: Start date of fuel consumption period (YYYY-MM-DD format)
          example: "2024-01-15"
        end_date:
          type: string
          format: date
          description: End date of fuel consumption period (YYYY-MM-DD format)
          example: "2024-01-15"
        facility_name:
          type: string
          description: Facility name where fuel was consumed
          maxLength: 200
          example: "Main Plant"
        fuel_type:
          type: string
          description: Type of fuel consumed
          maxLength: 200
          example: "Diesel"
        quantity:
          type: number
          description: Quantity of fuel consumed (must be > 0)
          minimum: 0.01
          example: 1000.50
        unit_of_measurement:
          type: string
          description: Unit of measurement for fuel quantity
          maxLength: 50
          example: "liters"
        subfacility:
          type: string
          description: Subfacility code (optional)
          maxLength: 100
          example: "BOILER-01"
        supplier_name:
          type: string
          description: Fuel supplier name (optional)
          maxLength: 200
          example: "PetroCo Inc"
        supplier_country:
          type: string
          description: Country of fuel supplier (optional)
          maxLength: 100
          example: "USA"

    Scope1FuelIngestRequest:
      type: object
      required: ["records"]
      properties:
        records:
          type: array
          items:
            $ref: "#/components/schemas/Scope1FuelRecord"
          minItems: 1
          maxItems: 1000
          description: Array of scope 1 fuel consumption records

    Scope1FuelIngestResponse:
      type: object
      properties:
        status:
          type: string
          enum: ["success"]
          description: Processing status
          example: "success"
        message:
          type: string
          description: Success message
          example: "Successfully processed 1 records across 1 facilities"
        data:
          type: object
          properties:
            sync_run_id:
              type: string
              description: Unique identifier for this sync run
              example: "6937e5b81dcdfab34c7a3cd5"
            import_type:
              type: string
              description: Type of import
              example: "scope1_fuel"
            total_records:
              type: integer
              description: Total number of records processed
              example: 1
            facilities_processed:
              type: array
              items:
                type: object
                properties:
                  facility_name:
                    type: string
                    description: Name of the facility
                    example: "Sample 1"
                  records_count:
                    type: integer
                    description: Number of records processed for this facility
                    example: 1
                  status:
                    type: string
                    description: Processing status for this facility
                    example: "success"
            upload_jobs_created:
              type: integer
              description: Number of upload jobs created
              example: 1
            upload_job_ids:
              type: array
              items:
                type: string
              description: List of upload job IDs
              example: ["6937e5b81dcdfab34c7a3cd6"]
            summary:
              type: object
              properties:
                total_facilities:
                  type: integer
                  description: Total number of facilities processed
                  example: 1
                total_records:
                  type: integer
                  description: Total number of records processed
                  example: 1
                successful_facilities:
                  type: integer
                  description: Number of facilities processed successfully
                  example: 1
                failed_facilities:
                  type: integer
                  description: Number of facilities that failed processing
                  example: 0

security:
  - BearerAuth: []

paths:
  /emissions/raw/:
    get:
      tags: [Analytics & Reporting]
      summary: Get raw emissions data
      description: |
        Retrieve raw emissions data with filtering, pagination, and export capabilities.

        This endpoint provides access to granular emissions data across all categories and data types. You can:

        - **Filter by data type**: Use `data_type`(required) parameter to get specific emission categories
        - **Filter by date range**: Use `date_from` and `date_to` for time-based filtering
        - **Filter by facilities**: Use `facility_ids` to get data for specific locations
        - **Filter by scope**: Use `scope` parameter (1, 2, 3) for emission scope filtering
        - **Filter by subfacility code**: Use `subfacility_code` parameter to filter specific subfacilities
        - **Export to CSV**: Set `format=csv` to get a download link for spreadsheet analysis

        The response includes detailed emission records with all relevant fields for the selected data type.
      parameters:
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/Authorization"
        - name: date_from
          in: query
          description: Start date (ISO 8601)
          required: false
          schema: { type: string, format: date }
        - name: date_to
          in: query
          description: End date (ISO 8601)
          required: false
          schema: { type: string, format: date }
        - name: facility_ids
          in: query
          description: Comma-separated facility (OrgStruct) IDs
          required: false
          schema: { type: string }
        - name: category
          in: query
          description: Emission category (e.g., "Fuel combustion")
          required: false
          schema: { type: string }
        - name: data_type
          in: query
          description: Data type/job type (e.g., trx, waste, emp_com, see /emissions/categories)
          required: true
          schema: { type: string }
        - name: subfacility_code
          in: query
          description: Subfacility code filter
          required: false
          schema: { type: string }
        - name: page
          in: query
          description: "Page number (default: 1)"
          required: false
          schema: { type: integer, minimum: 1, default: 1 }
        - name: limit
          in: query
          description: "Items per page (default: 100, max: 1000)"
          required: false
          schema: { type: integer, minimum: 1, maximum: 1000, default: 100 }
        - name: updated_since
          in: query
          description: Only records updated after this timestamp (ISO 8601)
          required: false
          schema: { type: string, format: date-time }
        - name: updated_to
          in: query
          description: Only records updated before this timestamp (ISO 8601)
          required: false
          schema: { type: string, format: date-time }
        - name: format
          in: query
          description: Set to 'csv' to receive a download link for CSV export
          required: false
          schema: { type: string, enum: [json, csv], default: json }
        - name: columns
          in: query
          description: Comma-separated list of column names to include in the response (e.g., "date,total_emission,business_facility_name,subfacility_code")
          required: false
          schema: { type: string }
      responses:
        "200":
          description: Raw emissions data
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: "#/components/schemas/EmissionRawResponse"
              examples:
                default:
                  summary: "Default transaction ('trx' data type)"
                  value:
                    data:
                      - file_name: ""
                        business_facility_name: "Mercutio Office"
                        uploader: "system@unravelcarbon.com"
                        _id: "689efca0ff6d9052499764cb"
                        updated_at: "2025-08-15 09:23:44.605000"
                        date: "2024-02-01 00:00:00"
                        scope: 3
                        total_emission: 39.61534179891021
                        scope_category: "NA"
                        sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_PGS: 39.61534179891021
                        sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_GOODS: 0.0
                        sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_NRG: 0
                        sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_U_TRANS: 0
                        sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_WASTE: 0
                        sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_BUSINESS: 0
                        sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_EMPLOY: 0
                        sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_U_LEASE: 0
                        sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_D_TRANS: 0
                        sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_PROCESS_SOLD: 0
                        sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_USE_SOLD: 0
                        sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_END_LIFE: 0
                        sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_D_LEASE: 0
                        sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_FRANCHISE: 0
                        sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_INVEST: 0
                        sub_scope_cat_dict.CO2_S3: 39.61534179891021
                        transaction_id: "38412847182318237.505663970"
                        secondary_transaction_id: "505663970"
                        business_model: "Indent"
                        item_description: "Crew Fashion T-Shirts"
                        supplier: "64a9483931a5c3dd041a0138"
                        total_price: 23.885944614465927
                        currency: "USD"
                        units: 1.0
                        unit_emission: 1.658521044
                        item_emission_factor_unit: "kg CO2-e/USD"
                        spend_category: "Textiles and textile products"
                        match: "exiobase"
                        product_category: "Clothing - Men"
                        product_subcategory: ""
                        material_composition_breakdown: []
                        capital_goods: false
                        act_measure_unit: "PC"
                        act_measure_value: 293.0
                        item_unit_weight: 0.15
                        trans_distance: 0.0
                        manufacturer_name: "Adidas"
                        manufacturer_location_of_origin: "Singapore"
                        item_ef_source: "411"
                        item_ef_name: "Wearing apparel; furs"
                        item_match_granularity: "category"
                        item_location_granularity: "continent"
                        company: "Alpha Squad Inc"
                    count: 21609
                    page: 1
                    limit: 1
                emp_com:
                  summary: "Employee commuting ('emp_com' data type)"
                  value:
                    data:
                      - _id: "657bc0816f84b635c88fd70b"
                        updated_at: "2023-12-15 02:57:04.987000"
                        begin_date: "2022-01-01 00:00:00"
                        end_date: "2022-12-31 00:00:00"
                        identifier: "a3cfc2fe-000d-41cf-810e-a377a9c3d7ed"
                        num_employee: 20
                        wfh_pct: 0
                        avg_distance: 1
                        date: "2022-01-02 00:00:00"
